NAME
    mv - move/rename a regular file

SYNOPSIS
    mv SRC DST

DESCRIPTION
    Renames SRC to DST. Implemented as copy-then-unlink because
    AdventFS doesn't yet expose a single rename syscall. The copy
    uses sys_fs_write's atomic sector-run swap, so the data side is
    safe: SRC stays whole until DST is fully durable.

    Refuses if DST already exists — there is no -f flag. Two-arg
    form only (no `mv SRC... DSTDIR`).

EXAMPLES
    mv draft.txt final.txt
    mv /tmp/build.log /var/log/build.log

EXIT STATUS
    0   success
    1   any failure. If the copy succeeded but the unlink failed,
        BOTH files are left in place; mv exits 1 and the user can
        decide which to remove. Better than the rename-and-lose
        case.

SEE ALSO
    cp(1), rm(1)

NOTES
    No -i (interactive), no -f (force overwrite), no multi-source
    form. Added in session 83.
